1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,020
The missing voice belonged to a woman who ran a tiny motel on the corridor between the station and the port.

2
00:00:06,020 --> 00:00:13,819
Her livelihood was the queue: a taxi, a tram, a trolley, and a cart all stopped at her door.

3
00:00:13,819 --> 00:00:18,013
“A vehicle is not a conveyance,” she said.

4
00:00:18,013 --> 00:00:30,741
“It is a promise that someone will come back.” Her face, when she said it, was entirely sincere, and she had been saying it for a year.

5
00:00:30,741 --> 00:00:34,076
The committee had never asked her anything.

6
00:00:34,076 --> 00:00:43,989
According to the plan, the new line would shut the corridor at night and serve only the far end of the district, leaving her one open hour.

7
00:00:43,989 --> 00:00:52,023
“We hereby revise nothing,” the introductory letter said, electronically and without sincerity.

8
00:00:52,023 --> 00:01:01,251
A recreational bicycle, a soccer ball, and a postcard from the kingdom of the north were the only things in her window.

9
00:01:01,251 --> 00:01:10,610
We had no automobile and no auto of any kind, and the fireplace in the waiting room had not been lit for a year.

10
00:01:10,610 --> 00:01:25,242
A psychologist from the exchange campus came with an exhaustive report: the sore shoulder of a passenger, the lazy habit of a distributor, and the inch of platform that made a wheelchair impossible.

11
00:01:25,242 --> 00:01:29,976
“A boat and an aircraft are both rooms,” she said.

12
00:01:29,976 --> 00:01:42,194
“The difference is where you keep the ax.” A volunteer would accompany her on the walk through the depot, and the depot was where the report had to be handed over.

13
00:01:42,194 --> 00:01:48,658
They were slightly late for the meeting, and the mortgage on the depot was due the same week.

14
00:01:48,658 --> 00:01:53,118
“We cannot mechanize a promise,” Maya said.

15
00:01:53,118 --> 00:02:12,789
“We can only mechanize a gate.” A ballet company travelled through with their costumes, a tram driver with forty years of service, and a taxi owner with a sore hand: all of them had signed the same petition, and all of them were available to speak.

16
00:02:12,789 --> 00:02:16,449
The instructive part was the queue itself.

17
00:02:16,449 --> 00:02:27,412
Together they measured it: so many seconds per person, so many horsepower per hour, and thereby a number that the committee could not ignore.

18
00:02:27,412 --> 00:02:41,205
“You must create one open position for the night run,” Aisha said, “including the stop that serves nobody but her.” And they bought the postcard, and put it in the report.

19
00:02:41,205 --> 00:02:54,180
Near the pond, a distributor of tickets would acquaint every new passenger with the rules, and the distributive effect of the new timetable was obvious in her ledger.
